From 620c2fed31cabcecb4df820c90b9bd9842984fc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 23:10:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Put the real roster in, and let a roster fix reach a running
 instance
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Thirteen real names off the handwritten sheet, each on their mentor's team, with
the starred name in each column recorded as that team's lead. The placeholder
flag is gone: a person is marked "no photo" when their photo field is empty,
which is one fewer thing that can fall out of step with itself.

Saved data beats seed data, which is right for everything except this — an
instance that had already run would have kept the fake names forever. So teams
now merge by id: a person nobody has touched takes their name from the seed, and
the moment a mentor scores them or the lead renames them the file's version is
theirs and the seed stops overriding. People added from the panel stay, and
people dropped from the seed stay too, because removing a real person is a
decision for the panel and not for a deploy.

The config files lost their Persian comments. Right-to-left text inside a .env
or a Caddyfile comes out scrambled in a terminal editor, and these three were
the only config files in the repo not written in English.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01U57HFy24nnB6PJ1Zmysc6j
